      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "T-S 13K2 3r +\u00a0Bodl. MS Heb. d 74/29r",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>\n<p>&hellip; from where it stops, it starts. And from which place does it stop? From</p>\n<p>Tuesday noon. Open</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p></p>\n<p>your eyes, colleagues, and see these tremendous contrivements. And let</p>\n<p>him not say that the Four</p>\n<p></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Gates only include a minority of days and hours, only four (week)days&mdash;</p>\n<p>because whoever says this,</p>\n<p></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>says it without knowledge and understanding. For the world rests on these</p>\n<p>(Gates) alone, and the correct dating of</p>\n<p></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>the festivals depends only on them. And his third argument, in which he</p>\n<p>said &lsquo;641</p>\n<p></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>on its day, 642 the next day&rsquo;, has no root in the words of the Sages, and even</p>\n<p>the one who originally contrived this (argument)</p>\n<p></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>and wrote it did not know his right hand from his left regarding the secret</p>\n<p>of the calendar, because he said that if Nisan is born</p>\n<p></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>on Sunday, Tuesday, or Thursday and Tishri on Tuesday, Thursday, or</p>\n<p>Sabbath until six hours, it is not postponed, (and if it is born) after six</p>\n<p>hours,</p>\n<p></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>it is postponed&mdash;and he did not notice that when Nisan is born on</p>\n<p>Sunday, Tuesday, or Thursday before six hours,</p>\n<p></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>the corresponding Tishri on Tuesday, Thursday or Sabbath will be after six</p>\n<p>hours, because there are between them two (week)days,</p>\n</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
